    <!-- Section 2: Biological Magnification & Ozone Layer -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>2. Biological Magnification &amp; Stratospheric Ozone Depletion</h2>

      <div class="grid two concept-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>☣️ Biological Magnification (Biomagnification)</h3>
          <p class="formula">Toxic Concentration increases progressively up the food chain: Producers &lt; Herbivores &lt; Carnivores &lt; Humans (Apex)</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Mechanism:</strong> Non-biodegradable synthetic agricultural chemicals (e.g., DDT, endosulfan, organochlorine pesticides, heavy metals like mercury and lead) wash into water bodies or soil.</li>
            <li><strong>Inability to Metabolize or Excrete:</strong> Because living organisms possess no biological catabolic enzymes to metabolize or void non-biodegradable chemicals, these fat-soluble toxins permanently accumulate inside adipose body tissues.</li>
            <li><strong>Maximum Concentration at Apex:</strong> Since human beings occupy the topmost position in multiple domestic and terrestrial food chains, the highest concentration of toxic chemical residue invariably accumulates within human bodies, causing neurotoxicity and endocrine disruptions.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🛡️ Stratospheric Ozone ($O_3$) &amp; Montreal Protocol</h3>
          <p class="formula">O₂ + UV &rarr; O + O &nbsp;|&nbsp; O + O₂ &rarr; O₃ &nbsp;|&nbsp; Cl• + O₃ &rarr; ClO• + O₂</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>The Ozone Shield:</strong> Ozone ($O_3$) at ground level is a lethal cellular poison, but in the stratosphere (15–30 km above Earth) it forms a crucial shield filtering lethal ultraviolet-B (UV-B) radiation. UV-B causes malignant melanoma (skin cancer), cataracts, damaged eye retinas, and kills marine phytoplankton.</li>
            <li><strong>Photochemical Formation:</strong> High-energy solar UV photons split molecular oxygen ($O_2$) into highly reactive nascent free oxygen atoms ($O$). A free oxygen atom then combines with molecular oxygen to generate ozone ($O_3$).</li>
            <li><strong>CFC Destruction Catalyst:</strong> Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs) from refrigerants and aerosol propellants rise into the stratosphere. UV breaks down CFCs to liberate chlorine free radicals ($Cl^\bullet$). A single chlorine radical catalytically destroys over 100,000 ozone molecules before being deactivated!</li>
            <li><strong>UNEP Montreal Protocol (1987):</strong> Historic international treaty where global nations agreed to freeze and phase out CFC production at 1986 levels, successfully halting Antarctic ozone hole expansion.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>

