        "Zooplankton",
        "Small Fish",
        "Fish-eating Bird"
      ],
      correct: 3,
      exp: "Because non-biodegradable chemicals cannot be metabolized or excreted, the organism at the apex trophic level (Fish-eating Bird) accumulates the highest biomagnified concentration."
    },
    {
      q: "Why does energy flow in an ecosystem occur strictly in a unidirectional manner?",
      opts: [
        "Energy captured by autotrophs does not revert back to the solar input, and energy passed to herbivores cannot return to autotrophs",
        "Decomposers pump energy directly back to the sun",
        "Carnivores give energy back to green plants",
        "Producers absorb energy from top predators"
      ],
      correct: 0,
      exp: "Energy flow is strictly unidirectional: solar energy captured by autotrophs never returns to the sun, and energy transferred from one trophic level to the next cannot flow backwards."
    },
    {
      q: "What role do decomposers (bacteria and saprophytic fungi) perform in an ecosystem?",
      opts: [
        "They capture solar energy to produce glucose",
        "They break down dead organic remains into simple inorganic substances that replenish the soil and biogeochemical cycles",
        "They convert oxygen into ozone",
        "They synthesize synthetic non-biodegradable polymers"
      ],
      correct: 1,
      exp: "Decomposers secrete extracellular digestive enzymes that break down complex dead organic tissue into simple inorganic minerals, ensuring natural nutrient recycling."
    },
